# Six companies, zero IPOs

The Chinese audio track was active for almost 15 years, from penguins FM to Xia branches, to Himalayans, which burned 10 years of money and four times a scale -- eventually bought for music at $18.6 billion, at a 40% discount.** No company was listed independently.**

This is the coldest fact of the track, more worthy of reading at the beginning than any growth figure.

The question to answer is: ** How high is the ceiling on this track?

