# Six "business diseases" in the Chinese Podcast industry

These are not the problems of a company, but the structural constraints of the entire track.

# Disease I: The user size is hard-bound

Chinese podcasts have a penetration rate of about **22%**, United States of America of about **50%**. There seems to be room, but one key difference is noticed -** Chinese users receive an average daily podcast of about 30 minutes, United States of America of about 60 minutes**.

This means that even if the penetration rate is up to the US, only half of the attention is devoted per person. On short video days, **2 hours +** in the Chinese market, the podcasts are fighting not for "the people who haven't listened to the podcasts," but for "the attention that has been filled with tremors/B stations/Small Red Books."

** ceiling calculations**: Long-term view, Chinese podcasting **150 - 2 billion** may be reasonable (currently about 100 million) and unlikely to reach 500 - 6 billion as short videos.

